        "original_id": "c3ed367b-8f7d-561a-8daa-28c3740bff9a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Fenwick, Northumberland; Bamburgh; Lindisfarne Castle; Chillingham Castle; Farne Islands; Northumberland; northeast coast of England\n- People: Sir Claudius Forster, 1st Baronet\n- Roles: Governors of Bamburgh Castle\n- Organizations: the Crown\n\nFacts:\n- In 1609, the Crown granted Sir Claudius Forster, 1st Baronet, ownership of Bamburgh Castle and its estates.\n- Sir Claudius Forster, 1st Baronet, was descended from a long line of Governors of Bamburgh Castle.\n- Bamburgh Castle is a castle on the northeast coast of England by the village of Bamburgh in Northumberland.\n- Fenwick, Northumberland, is close to Lindisfarne Castle, Bamburgh Castle, and Chillingham Castle.\n- Fenwick, Northumberland, is an ideal base for exploring the history of Northumberland and the Farne Islands.",
